  "onboardingTitle1": "How it works",
  "onboardingBody1": "Each heartbeat slightly changes the colour of your skin as blood volume changes. These changes are far too small to see, but a camera can pick them up. This technique is called remote photoplethysmography (rPPG).",
  "onboardingTitle2": "Light and stillness matter",
  "onboardingBody2": "The signal is tiny, so movement, talking, changing light, screen flicker and strong backlight can easily overwhelm it. Sit still in soft, even, front-facing light for best results.",
  "onboardingTitle3": "What this app can and cannot do",
  "onboardingBody3": "It estimates heart rate in beats per minute when the signal passes quality checks. It does not measure blood pressure, oxygen saturation, glucose, temperature or stress, and it cannot detect or rule out any medical condition.",
  "onboardingTitle4": "Your data stays on this device",
  "onboardingBody4": "Video is processed on the device and is never recorded, saved or uploaded. Only measurement summaries you choose to save are stored locally, and you can export or delete them at any time.",
  "onboardingAcknowledge": "I understand these results are experimental estimates and are not medical advice.",
